From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:17:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: switch the IWLAN transport on for Wi-Fi calling

The modem takes the Wi-Fi calling configuration and then does nothing with it: the IMS log shows
wifi_call: 2 and wfc_preference = 3 stored and acknowledged, and no ePDG registration is ever
attempted, so isVowifiEnabled stays false and a forced WFC call reports "connect to a wireless
network" while connected to one.

persist.data.iwlan.enable is the QTI switch for the IWLAN data path an ePDG tunnel rides on. Stock
sets it on this device and this port did not carry it over, which fits the symptom exactly:
configuration accepted, transport switched off, nothing to register over.

persist.radio.app_hw_mbn_path comes from the same diff of stock's build.prop. It points the modem at
the hardware MBN configs on /firmware, which is the stock modem partition and untouched by this
build, so the path is stock's own.

persist.radio.VT_CAM_INTERFACE is deliberately not copied: video telephony is switched off and
cannot work here regardless.
---
 device.mk | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/device.mk b/device.mk
index d2d6d0f..9fd9b18 100644
--- a/device.mk
+++ b/device.mk
@@ -391,6 +391,25 @@ PRODUCT_PACKAGES += libshim_vtsurface
 # want to avoid blocking the binder thread".
 PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += ro.telephony.block_binder_thread_on_incoming_calls=false
 
+# Two properties the stock 7.1 ROM sets on this exact device and we did not carry over. Found by
+# diffing stock's build.prop against ours while chasing Wi-Fi calling.
+#
+# persist.data.iwlan.enable is the QTI switch for the IWLAN data path, which is what an ePDG tunnel
+# rides on. Without it the modem accepts the Wi-Fi calling configuration -- the log shows
+# wifi_call: 2 and wfc_preference 3 stored and acknowledged -- and then never attempts to register,
+# because the transport it would use is switched off. That matches the symptom exactly: WFC config
+# accepted, no IWLAN registration, isVowifiEnabled=false.
+#
+# persist.radio.app_hw_mbn_path tells the modem where to find its hardware MBN configs. /firmware is
+# the stock modem partition and untouched by this build, so the path is stock's own; a path that did
+# not exist would behave the same as leaving it unset.
+#
+# Note what is NOT copied: persist.radio.VT_CAM_INTERFACE, because video telephony is deliberately
+# off (config_device_vt_available, above) and cannot work regardless.
+PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += \
+    persist.data.iwlan.enable=true \
+    persist.radio.app_hw_mbn_path=/firmware/image/modem_pr/mcfg/configs/mcfg_hw/generic/common/MSM8994/LA
+
 # nanopb 0.2.8, for libril-qc-qmi-1.so alone. See nanopb-0.2.8/Android.bp for why a second copy of
 # nanopb has to exist at all.
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += libnanopb_legacy
